      "message": "the feature only really makes sense with `--no-squash`. some 90+% of people use the `--squash` workflow, where all local commits are collapsed into one commit on Gerrit. if you\u0027d want independent commits with independent bypass footers, the standard solution would be to use stacked branches (`git new-branch`). each change is its own branch, has its own description, passes presubmit independently locally, and passes independently on CQ (without needing to change `depot_tools` at all)",
